      "title": "A little background.",
      "href": "daniel.html#story",
      "text": "The person behind the record A little background. Daniel Caesar is the stage name of Ashton Dumar Norwill Simmonds, a Canadian singer and songwriter born in 1995. His music combines R&B with soul and gospel, often bringing questions of love, belief and personal identity into intimate vocal performances. He first built an audience through the independent EPs Praise Break (2014) and Pilgrim's Paradise (2015). His debut studio album, Freudian (2017), brought international recognition and Grammy nominations. Best Part, his collaboration with H.E.R., won the 2019 Grammy for Best R&B Performance. CASE STUDY 01 followed in 2019, then NEVER ENOUGH in 2023. The latter contains Let Me Go, the focus of this artist study, and Cool. His fourth studio album, Son Of Spergy (2025), turns toward family, faith and reconciliation; Who Knows and Sins Of The Father appear on that record. Biographical background: Wikipedia / Daniel Caesar \u2197 A little context Finding a voice. Three useful moments, rather than a complete biography. A question to carry into the music When the title phrase returns, does its gentle delivery make the request feel more certain, or reveal how difficult it is to say? The focus track below provides one way into that question. These notes describe audible choices and offer a personal reading, rather than claiming to reveal the artist's private intentions. Read the focus study \u2192",
